1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:03,200
A red face.

2
00:00:03,465 --> 00:00:05,207
A very long nose.

3
00:00:05,507 --> 00:00:09,059
Wings on the back, and a fan
of feathers in one hand.

4
00:00:09,359 --> 00:00:14,030
This is the tengu, the mountain
goblin of Japanese legend.

5
00:00:14,330 --> 00:00:18,425
Its name is written with two
characters that mean "heavenly

6
00:00:18,425 --> 00:00:22,096
dog." Yet the tengu we know
looks nothing like a dog.

7
00:00:22,396 --> 00:00:25,444
And in the oldest
Japanese record, the tengu

8
00:00:25,444 --> 00:00:28,421
is not a creature of the mountains at all.

9
00:00:28,721 --> 00:00:30,685
It is something in the sky.

10
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:36,204
In this episode, we follow
the tengu from a court chronicle

11
00:00:36,204 --> 00:00:40,410
of the year 720, through
medieval tales, to the masks,

12
00:00:40,410 --> 00:00:44,061
carvings, and printed
books of later centuries.

13
00:00:49,467 --> 00:00:55,536
The Nihon Shoki, the Chronicles
of Japan, was completed in 720.

14
00:00:55,836 --> 00:01:00,751
Its entry for the year 637
records a strange event.

15
00:01:01,051 --> 00:01:06,534
A great star flowed across the sky from
east to west, with a sound like thunder.

16
00:01:06,834 --> 00:01:10,343
Some people said it
was the sound of a falling star.

17
00:01:10,643 --> 00:01:13,160
Others said it was thunder from the earth.

18
00:01:14,067 --> 00:01:19,645
Then a Buddhist monk named Bin, who had
studied in China, gave a different answer.

19
00:01:19,945 --> 00:01:22,507
It is not a falling star, he said.

20
00:01:22,807 --> 00:01:28,567
It is a tengu, a celestial dog, and the
sound of its barking is like thunder.

21
00:01:28,867 --> 00:01:33,835
This is thought to be the first time
the word appears in a Japanese record.

22
00:01:34,767 --> 00:01:37,327
Bin was drawing on Chinese learning.

23
00:01:37,627 --> 00:01:41,892
In the Records of the Grand
Historian, written in China more

24
00:01:41,892 --> 00:01:46,446
than two thousand years ago,
the heavenly dog is a kind of star.

25
00:01:46,746 --> 00:01:50,291
It looks like a great shooting
star, it makes a sound,

26
00:01:50,291 --> 00:01:53,835
and where it comes down
to earth, it looks like a dog.

27
00:01:54,135 --> 00:01:58,955
Today, we might call such a sight
a fireball, a very bright meteor.

28
00:01:59,867 --> 00:02:03,354
In one old copy of the chronicle,
a small reading

29
00:02:03,354 --> 00:02:06,551
note beside the word
calls it a heavenly fox.

30
00:02:06,851 --> 00:02:12,085
After this, the word almost disappears
from the records for several centuries.

31
00:02:15,367 --> 00:02:18,129
When the tengu returns, it has changed.

32
00:02:18,429 --> 00:02:22,356
In the Konjaku Monogatari,
a great collection of tales

33
00:02:22,356 --> 00:02:25,763
from the twelfth century,
tengu deceive people,

34
00:02:25,763 --> 00:02:29,838
and try to lead Buddhist monks
away from their practice.

35
00:02:30,138 --> 00:02:34,863
They are proud and clever,
and in the end, they are usually defeated.

36
00:02:35,767 --> 00:02:40,009
In one tale, a Buddha appears
in the branches of a persimmon

37
00:02:40,009 --> 00:02:43,677
tree in the capital, shining
and scattering flowers.

38
00:02:43,977 --> 00:02:45,855
Crowds come to worship.

39
00:02:46,155 --> 00:02:49,974
But one minister has his doubts,
and he simply keeps staring.

40
00:02:50,274 --> 00:02:53,111
At last the Buddha vanishes, and a great

41
00:02:53,111 --> 00:02:56,160
kite with a broken wing
falls from the tree.

42
00:02:56,460 --> 00:02:58,743
The tengu was a bird all along.

43
00:02:59,667 --> 00:03:04,625
In another tale, a tengu from China
crosses the sea to test the monks

44
00:03:04,625 --> 00:03:09,583
of Japan, and is badly beaten
by the young attendants who guard them.

45
00:03:09,883 --> 00:03:15,486
Picture scrolls of the 1200s
and 1300s retold such stories,

46
00:03:15,486 --> 00:03:21,764
and many of their tengu have
the beaks and wings of birds of prey.

47
00:03:22,064 --> 00:03:26,635
The Tengu Zōshi,
from around 1296, even shows

48
00:03:26,635 --> 00:03:31,621
proud monks as tengu,
as a warning against pride.

49
00:03:31,921 --> 00:03:37,253
This bird-faced form lives on today
as the karasu tengu, the "crow tengu."

50
00:03:39,067 --> 00:03:45,311
Over time, another kind of tengu became
familiar: a red face, a long nose, and the

51
00:03:45,311 --> 00:03:51,709
dress of a yamabushi, one of the mountain
ascetics of Japan, with a fan of feathers.

52
00:03:52,009 --> 00:03:55,847
Exactly when the long nose
first appeared is not clear.

53
00:03:56,147 --> 00:04:00,958
This mask, made for a suit
of armor in the early 1700s,

54
00:04:00,958 --> 00:04:04,879
already gives the tengu
a long, jutting nose.

55
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:10,757
Mount Kurama, north of Kyoto,
became famous for its great tengu.

56
00:04:11,057 --> 00:04:17,350
A Noh play, Kurama Tengu, tells how the
young Minamoto no Yoshitsune, then called

57
00:04:17,350 --> 00:04:23,171
Ushiwakamaru, learned the arts of war
from the great tengu of the mountain.

58
00:04:23,471 --> 00:04:27,643
Edo-period artists returned
to this scene again and again,

59
00:04:27,643 --> 00:04:30,937
in prints and in small
carvings like this one.

60
00:04:31,867 --> 00:04:33,905
And the bird never went away.

61
00:04:34,205 --> 00:04:36,889
In this book of sketches by Hokusai,

62
00:04:36,889 --> 00:04:40,467
the figure labeled "tengu"
is still a great bird.

63
00:04:40,767 --> 00:04:46,374
For centuries, long-nosed tengu
and bird-faced tengu lived side by side.

64
00:04:46,674 --> 00:04:50,041
Over time, tengu also became guardians.

65
00:04:50,341 --> 00:04:53,358
At some mountain temples
and shrines, they are

66
00:04:53,358 --> 00:04:56,643
still honored as protectors
of the mountain today.

67
00:04:58,467 --> 00:05:00,430
So what was the first tengu?

68
00:05:00,730 --> 00:05:05,134
In the oldest record, it is a star
that roared across the sky.

69
00:05:05,434 --> 00:05:10,519
In medieval tales, it is a bird
that deceives and tests the faithful.

70
00:05:10,819 --> 00:05:16,299
The long-nosed figure came later, and
joined the bird rather than replacing it.

71
00:05:18,133 --> 00:05:22,623
The tengu we picture today is not
the oldest part of the legend.

72
00:05:22,923 --> 00:05:24,823
It is one of the newest.

73
00:05:25,123 --> 00:05:27,451
Every story has an origin.

74
00:05:27,751 --> 00:05:30,407
Sometimes, it begins in the sky.

75
